── detail · density ──
How the messages of a thread, the detail pane and a direct message are laid out.

compact  in use
One line a message: the time, the author in a column, then the text. The author is left blank for the same person within five minutes. A thin line marks a new day, and a thread's replies sit under one divider. In a narrow panel the author and time take a line and the text sits under it.

cozy
The roomier layout: the author, place and date on a line, the text under it, the reactions on a line of their own, a blank line between messages, and replies two cells in.

config: [slack] density = "compact" or "cozy"
── status · SETTINGS ──
PgUp/PgDn scroll  q quit  x extra actions  ~ notices  ←→↑↓ navigate
